Visual Promt Studio 1.1
For this challenge, imagine you are a lead graphic designer hired by a movie studio.
The director wants you to create a promotional film poster that establishes a
distinct visual mood for an upcoming science fiction blockbuster.

-Vocab Breakdown-

Lines- Most basic element in visual art- directs the eye, outlines shapes, and implies movement

Shape- The form an object takes within the image

Texture- How an object appears to feel when touched. (smooth, rough, hard, soft)

Volume- how much space an object tzkes up 

Contrast- the way and object/color does/does not stand out in relation to other things around it 



Reflection- In my movie poster the lines are implying movement through the trails behind the whale. They also draw the viewers’ eye toward the whale with the blue pattern on its body, as well as create texture on its belly. The lines are one of the most prominent visual elements in the picture, second only to the volume of the whale. Its massive scale is made evident by the fact that it dwarfs the skyscrapers beneath it. However, it still is not as big as I had intended in the original image prompt. I wanted it to be even bigger than what is shown, as if it could swallow the entire city in its mouth. I also wanted the whale to look more machine-like than it does. In my mind it was less life-like and looked like it needed to be piloted. After tweaking these two things I found that the image changed in tone. It went from the whale looking like a benevolent thing, to it looking like a weapon.
